Named demons are indeed "meditating", just like quest nemeses and
unlike nymphs. They will wake up if you are in line of sight or if
they are damaged. In case you want to wake up Asmodeus with a drum of
earthquake, I made a graph of its range: http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Drum_o=
f_earthquake

In case you want to take him down the stairs, just don't engrave
Elbereth at any time. "Fleeing" demons won't follow, and it take quite
some time for that condition to wear off.

IMHO, Asmodeus is a pretty bad example to go through all this trouble
for.  You can just xorn in into his lair and take him out, or instead
pay him off once he appears naturally.


